#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:5
#: b27ebafa9fd5403bb45be7b0c9a38f4b
msgid "GCS Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:6
#: b5ea6737c3634ff4a9719ee9be62e9f5
msgid "Significant improvements have been made in Copter-4.0 and later for Ground Control Failsafe ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:8
#: 6921b75f28c7460195b2715393982dc0
msgid "The Ground Station Control (GCS) failsafe controls how Copter will behave if contact with the GCS is lost.  The GCS failsafe monitors the time since the last MAVLink heartbeat from the GCS.  If no heartbeat is received :ref:`FS_GCS_TIMEOUT<FS_GCS_TIMEOUT>` seconds (Default is 5 seconds), the GCS failsafe event will trigger based on your parameter settings. Note that if no GCS is ever connected, the GCS failsafe will remain inactive regardless of parameter settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:12
#: 376ad90a828b4f7b95087886bc6edcf8
msgid "Copter also supports other failsafes: :ref:`Radio <radio-failsafe>`, :ref:`Battery <failsafe-battery>`, and :ref:`EKF / DCM Check <ekf-inav-failsafe>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:15
#: ef1cbb73f8ef46d19d3c4dfbcddcc459
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:17
#: d9ebd332d373417791fffbd569e58bfe
msgid "The following situations can cause a loss of GCS MAVLink heartbeat, triggering a GCS failsafe event after :ref:`FS_GCS_TIMEOUT<FS_GCS_TIMEOUT>` seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:19
#: 2d835a9766ea43acbbbffa3eb5abeb67
msgid "The operator turns off or otherwise disconnects the GCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:20
#: 2c122fa14a524f02abb322f6b1c6b471
msgid "The copter travels beyond the range of the  GCS telemetry radios"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:21
#: 6011f302fadd46308640529ce9c81b69
msgid "The GCS telemetry radio on either end loses power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:22
#: 22bfdc030c7f4cea82a1f1f3255056fa
msgid "Wires connecting the GCS telemetry radio to the autopilot or ground equipment become disconnected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:25
#: c0b4842fa893464fa2924df39419ddba
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:27
#: 0ef8126f19454c90ab5bfec9e10bacee
msgid "When a GCS failsafe is triggered, the copter can be configured via parameters to do nothing, land immediately, RTL, or SmartRTL.  It can also be configured to bypass the failsafe in an Auto Mode mission, bypass the failsafe in pilot controlled modes, or to continue landing if already in a landing phase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:29
#: e2e3e48651d744f9b7cf029f744e650f
msgid "If the copter is disarmed, no failsafe will take place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:30
#: 31495dd5670d43d8977ed96c200c34da
msgid "If the copter is armed but has landed, the copter will immediately disarm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:31
#: b035e9d674914e79a83d40bfedbe919d
msgid "If the copter is armed in Stabilize or Acro modes, and the throttle input is at minimum, the copter will immediately disarm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:32
#: 566297c3ad414a63aa78a64221694787
msgid "Otherwise, the copter will take the actions as configured in the parameters described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:34
#: 5fbccb05f7c64992a6f2e224fa5bea26
msgid "If the failsafe clears (i.e. GCS reconnects and MAVLink heartbeat is restored) the copter will remain in its failsafe mode. It will **not** automatically return to the flight mode that was active before the failsafe was triggered. This means that if, for example, the vehicle was in Loiter when the failsafe occurred and the flight mode was automatically changed to RTL, even after the GCS reconnects, the vehicle would remain in RTL.  If the pilot wished to re-take control in Loiter he/she would need to change the flight mode switch to another position and then back to Loiter. This can be done via the re-connected GCS also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:37
#: 747e2316cd0d46e2abd500cebec9b611
msgid "Setting the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:39
#: e0a18b69f2b14ad79957ac4d213100b6
msgid "In Mission Planner's  full parameter list or full parameter tree, set the :ref:`FS_GCS_ENABLE <FS_GCS_ENABLE>` parameter to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:41
#: b3020accb9c341d98ec98a8bff5a4274
msgid "**Disabled** (Value 0) will disable the GCS failsafe entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:42
#: dfdebdc63e964c0daf65633edd831344
msgid "**Enabled Always RTL** (Value 1) will switch the copter to RTL Mode.  If the GPS position is not usable, the copter will change to Land Mode instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:43
#: 080ffdfc7c3c44f58f322db553219287
msgid "**Enabled Continue with Mission in Auto Mode (this value has no effect in 4.0 and later with FS_OPTION parameter replacing function, see below )** (Value 2) will ignore the failsafe in an Auto Mode mission. Otherwise, it will behave the same as *Enabled Always RTL*. This option no longer exists in Copter 4.0 and later. Instead, see the :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` parameter for this function. Setting this value in Copter 4.0 and later version will automatically be converted and set to Value 1 (Always RTL) and the :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` bitmask will be modified to include bit (1) for \"Continue auto mode mission on GCS failsafe\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:44
#: fd23494eb0584ff4803e47277b642564
msgid "**Enabled SmartRTL or RTL** (Value 3) will switch the copter to SmartRTL mode. If SmartRTL is not available, the copter will switch to RTL Mode instead.  If the GPS position is not usable, the copter will change to Land Mode instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:45
#: f7b5c43e4362445e83787aa6175f8e3a
msgid "**Enabled SmartRTL or Land** (Value 4) will switch the copter to SmartRTL mode. If SmartRTL is not available, the copter will switch to Land Mode instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:46
#: 4ce84d06f35c47bd83beaffb2d429395
msgid "**Enabled Always Land** (Value 5) will switch the copter to Land Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:47
#: 38a9f614d22d4f9c9faf91c8f049453f
msgid "**Auto DO_LAND_START or RTL** (Value 6) will execute a DO_LAND_START auto mission sequence or and RTL if no DO_LAND_START sequence exists(see :ref:`common-do-land-start`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:48
#: 8c9a4daeed8e4e0dae8867e099354f48
msgid "**BRAKE or LAND** (Value 7): switch to BRAKE mode if included in firmware or to LAND mode, if not included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:49
#: 471f53ca7aef470a9694c571bff01fab
msgid "Any invalid value (Such as accidentally enter 99 as a parameter value) will will behave the same as **Enabled Always RTL**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:51
#: 1640dc87b28847dca38adcd210c37bca
msgid "The :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` parameter (Copter 4.0 and later) is a bitmask parameter to select one or more options that modify the standard actions of the radio, GCS, and battery failsafe. In the Mission Planner full parameter list or full parameter tree, the handy checkbox popup window is an easy what to set this (and any other bitmask) parameter. Be sure to go to Help > Check Beta Updates to pull the latest parameter definitions first while connected to the internet. The :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` bits are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:53
#: bd14cfa2d26d460a95d2023706d8b996
msgid "bit 0 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:54
#: 7d14898c135248fe9df45947e84c92ec
msgid "bit 1 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Ground Control Station Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:55
#: 369c385b3e7445778fd2df9215278ab0
msgid "bit 2 set: Continue if in guided mode :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:56
#: 0735141c69854d6183cc163d77ff0791
msgid "bit 3 set: Continue if landing on any failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:57
#: 235f1b5357884250b1aaaad43c30c689
msgid "bit 4 set: Continue in pilot control on :ref:`Ground Control Station Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:58
#: e7029de840dc44d69c3adbf0f3023bde
msgid "bit 5 set: Release gripper during failsafe handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:59
#: a6cda079111f4d989c5c97f3bdf24425
msgid "If none of the above are set, then execute the :ref:`FS_GCS_ENABLE <FS_GCS_ENABLE>` option as configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:61
#: 106ab92d917a495eb2dee5ee6e5f2fc8
msgid "Only bitmask bits 1, 3, 4 & 5 affect actions taken during GCS failsafe. This parameter also works in conjunction with the battery and radio failsafe, so ensure you are taking all options into account when setting this parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:68
#: e8a354679e884b438200aa38aa7be4f9
msgid "All Failsafe Parameters can be observed or set from the Advanced Parameter List in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""
